## Why This Is Asked

This question tests your ability to translate security policy into concrete technical controls and incident response processes across DevOps and security teams.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege IAM roles for each microservice
- S3 Data Events and CloudTrail for comprehensive auditing
- Open Policy Agent for policy enforcement at API gateway
- Infrastructure as Code guardrails and CI/CD security checks
- Incident response playbooks with measurable success metrics

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-logs-${aws:userid}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:userid}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical analytics isolation in a multi-tenant fintech environment, focusing on tenant boundaries, masking, catalog governance, and IR collaboration.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant analytics boundaries (schemas or secure views)
- Dynamic data masking for PII in dashboards
- ABAC with tenant context for dataset access
- Immutable audit logs and data catalog tagging
- IR playbooks with defined SLAs and measurable metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
function authorize(userTenant, dataset) {
  if (!dataset.tenants.includes(userTenant)) {
    throw new Error('Access denied');
  }
  // enforce masking in downstream queries via protected views
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test and validate tenant isolation in BI dashboards?
- What metrics indicate effective containment and data-loss prevention?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical application of confidential computing to multi-tenant isolation in real-time ML workloads, beyond token-based controls.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (TDX/Nitro/SEV)
- Per-tenant attested enclaves and key management
- Envelope encryption of in-flight data and outputs
- Attestation-based admission control at API gateway
- IR playbook with measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-spec showing attestation flow
function attestedInference(req, enclave) {
  if (!enclave.attest(req.tenant)) throw new Error('Untrusted tenant');
  const input = enclave.declassify(req.input, req.tenant);
  const out = enclave.infer(input);
  return enclave.envelope(out, req.tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without service downtime?
- How would you detect and respond to a compromised enclave?
